c) Analytics for the ID path

Where you already call track():

On ID “Lookup” CTA: track('guardian_link_attempt', { method: 'id' });

On /api/students/searchById error: track('guardian_link_failure', { method: 'id', reason: serverCode });

On createLink(...,'id') → success/pendings: same events as code/qr paths.

d) i18n keys (add to vi/en)
{
  "link": {
    "id": {
      "placeholder": "Enter Student ID",
      "cta": "Find student"
    }
  }
}

e) Error mapping (extend your switch)
function mapError(code?: string) {
  switch (code) {
    case 'INVALID_CODE':
    case 'EXPIRED_CODE':
    case 'MAX_USES_REACHED':
      return 'link.error.invalid';
    case 'TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS':
      return 'link.error.tooMany';
    case 'NOT_FOUND':
      return 'link.error.invalid';
    case 'ALREADY_LINKED':
      return 'link.error.already';
    default:
      return 'link.error.invalid';
  }
}

2) Server tests (Functions) — minimal but meaningful

Create functions/test/guardian.spec.ts (using Jest + supertest). If you don’t have supertest yet:

npm i -D jest ts-jest supertest @types/jest @types/supertest


functions/jest.config.js:

module.exports = {
  testEnvironment: 'node',
  testMatch: ['**/test/**/*.spec.ts'],
  transform: { '^.+\\.tsx?$': ['ts-jest', { tsconfig: 'tsconfig.json' }] },
};


Example tests:

import request from 'supertest';
import * as admin from 'firebase-admin';

// Helper to mint an ID token for test user (use emulator or a fixed test token)
async function getTokenFor(uid: string) {
  // With emulator, you can sign a custom token then exchange; else stub a header in dev-only routes.
  const custom = await admin.auth().createCustomToken(uid);
  // In emulator tests, you can allow custom tokens or mock middleware.
  return custom; // replace with real idToken if needed
}

describe('Guardian linking endpoints', () => {
  const base = 'http://127.0.0.1:5001/<PROJECT>/<REGION>/api'; // emulator URL

  it('lookupCode returns masked preview for valid code', async () => {
    const token = await getTokenFor('test-guardian-uid');
    const res = await request(base)
      .post('/api/guardian/lookupCode')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`)
      .send({ code: 'ABC123' });
    expect([200,404,410]).toContain(res.status);
    if (res.status === 200) {
      expect(res.body.ok).toBe(true);
      expect(res.body.student).toHaveProperty('fullNameInitials');
      expect(res.body.student).not.toHaveProperty('dob');
    }
  });

  it('createLink is idempotent', async () => {
    const token = await getTokenFor('test-guardian-uid');
    const first = await request(base)
      .post('/api/guardian/createLink')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`)
      .send({ studentId: 'stu_1', method: 'code' });
    expect(first.body.ok).toBe(true);
    const linkId = first.body.link.id;

    const second = await request(base)
      .post('/api/guardian/createLink')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`)
      .send({ studentId: 'stu_1', method: 'code' });
    expect(second.body.ok).toBe(true);
    expect(second.body.link.id).toBe(linkId);
  });

  it('getLinkById returns terminal status after approval', async () => {
    const token = await getTokenFor('test-guardian-uid');
    const res = await request(base)
      .post('/api/guardian/getLinkById')
      .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`)
      .send({ linkId: 'lnk_1' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(200);
    expect(res.body.link).toHaveProperty('status');
  });
});


Tip: If you’re not on the emulator, mock the auth middleware and call the underlying handlers with a fake uid. The goal is to smoke the contracts, not to build a full integration rig today.

3) Client UI tests (React Native Testing Library)

Install:

npm i -D @testing-library/react-native @testing-library/jest-native jest


app/(onboarding)/__tests__/guardian-link.spec.tsx:

import React from 'react';
import { render, fireEvent, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react-native';
import GuardianLink from '../guardian-link';

jest.mock('@/services/backend.guardian', () => ({
  lookupCode: jest.fn(async (code: string) =>
    code === 'GOOD123'
      ? { ok: true, student: { id: 'stu1', fullNameInitials: 'N. A.', grade: '5' } }
      : { ok: false, code: 'INVALID_CODE' }
  ),
  createLink: jest.fn(async () => ({ ok: true, link: { id: 'lnk1', status: 'active' } })),
}));

test('Code tab: lookup → preview → confirm', async () => {
  const { getByPlaceholderText, getByText, queryByText } = render(<GuardianLink />);

  fireEvent.press(getByText('Code'));
  fireEvent.changeText(getByPlaceholderText('Enter invite code'), 'GOOD123');
  fireEvent.press(getByText('Lookup'));

  await waitFor(() => expect(queryByText('Confirm & Link')).toBeTruthy());
  fireEvent.press(getByText('Confirm & Link'));
  // Expect navigation or success message — depending on your router mocks
});


You can add a similar test for the ID tab once wired to searchStudentById.

